crt-pi shader — original source and license
==========================================

Original shader: crt-pi.glsl from libretro/glsl-shaders
Repository: https://github.com/libretro/glsl-shaders
Path: crt/shaders/crt-pi.glsl
Author: Copyright (C) 2015-2016 davej
License: GNU General Public License v2 (or later) — see header in crt-pi.glsl

This copy is retained verbatim (with added uniform-parameter docs) under
its original GPL-2.0+ license.

Project note (play-crt):
  The user request described crt-pi as "MIT, Raspberry Pi CRT shader".
  The upstream file is actually GPL-2.0+. This repository keeps the
  original GPL-2.0+ header intact in assets/shaders/crt-pi.glsl and
  lists the shader under GPL-2.0+ in README.md. The Rust port in
  src/crt_pi.rs implements the same algorithm and is covered by the
  project's MIT license (algorithm itself is not copyrightable; the GLSL
  text remains GPL-2.0+).

  If you redistribute the .glsl verbatim, you must comply with GPL-2.0+.
  If you only use the Rust port (CPU fallback / glow path loads the GLSL
  at runtime), note the runtime dependency on the GPL-2.0+ shader text.

See also: https://github.com/libretro/glsl-shaders/blob/master/crt/shaders/crt-pi.glsl
